Cycle 6 is complete. One analysis was run synchronously, results are filled in, and the findings entry is appended.

**What I did**

- Posed a new regime/meta question from the free slot: if the reaccel edge is regime-dependent as Charter D2 claims, then performance itself should persist in time (good weeks following good weeks). Pre-registered it in the docstring of `AUREL_RESEARCH/scripts/c6_persistence.py` before looking at numbers.
- Ran it on the existing 19404-trade scan cache only. No scan, no M5 load, no MT5, no external calls. Runtime was 162 s.

**Result: null, all three predictions failed**

| Window | Weekly lag-1 autocorr of mean R | One-sided permutation p | Trailing 4-week split, Welch t |
|---|---|---|---|
| In 2010–20 | −0.059 | 0.91 | −1.07 |
| Out 2021–26H1 | −0.032 | 0.69 | +0.03 |
| Recent 2024–26H1 | −0.120 | 0.90 | −0.19 |

The positive control worked: weekly setup counts autocorrelate strongly, with lag-1 r between +0.42 and +0.62 and permutation p below 0.002. So the method detects persistence where it exists, and mean R simply has none at the week or month scale. A variance decomposition showed the spread of weekly and monthly mean R is fully explained by trade-level sampling noise. Any regime-driven swing in the true weekly mean is bounded at roughly 0.02 to 0.03 R, the same size as execution cost.

**Strongest counter-argument recorded**: the out-of-sample monthly trailing split came in at +0.05 R with t 1.9, and recent-window monthly TP-rate persists while mean R does not. In-sample has the opposite sign and this is one cell of six, so it is logged as low-priority for a single pre-registered check once 12+ months of post-2026-07 data exist.

**Knowledge gained and recorded**

- "Read the regime from recent performance" has no information. The R-based regime meter and equity-curve on/off ideas are closed in the backlog.
- If the recent-years edge is real, it shows up only as a level difference between windows, not as a persistent state. A regime meter must therefore use external state, which raises the priority of the intraday dollar and rates data need already in DATA_MAP §6.
- Added methodology item 7 to the backlog header: time-series nulls must carry a positive control and a variance decomposition.

